My strategy involves choosing a USD currency pair that has been in an uptrend for at least 3 months (bullish trend).
When the pair is at the bottom of its range (lower band of price action), I use algorithms to time entries and exits (if needed) at the high end of the range.
I don't use stop losses — I sell if the macro thesis no longer holds or the trend breaks down to neutral instead of bullish.
I normally target trades where a macro theme is in place, such as in October 2025 when the new Japanese prime minister was elected, pledging rate drops and fiscal stimulus, leading to yen depreciation.
In this case, with a >3-month bullish trend in USD/JPY and price at the lower range, it provided an opportunity for larger position sizing than normal trades.
The currency pairs I trade are USD/EUR, USD/GBP, CAD/USD, and USD/JPY.
